font-family: var(--tagline-font);
letter-spacing:3px;
text-transform:uppercase;
color:#7db7d6;]Day 1: Clear Weather — Akala West Coast[/div]
We begin on the west side of Akala Island, heading north until we catch the eastbound current.


Easy start. Get your balance. Feel the ocean.


[div=
margin-top:6px;
font-size: var(--tagline-size);
font-family: var(--tagline-font);
letter-spacing:3px;
text-transform:uppercase;
color:#7db7d6;]Day 2: Harsh Sunlight — Akala Northeast[/div]
We ride the current southward, circling the northeast coast of Akala.


The Moon-Tide Parade comes to an end.


[div=
margin-top:6px;
font-size: var(--tagline-size);
font-family: var(--tagline-font);
letter-spacing:3px;
text-transform:uppercase;
color:#7db7d6;]Day 3: Heavy Rain — Ula’ula Northeast[/div]
We sweep down along Ula’ula’s northeastern coast.


Surfers have the chance to dock at Malie City — rest, recover, or explore the gardens, just make it back before we set off!


[div=
margin-top:6px;
font-size: var(--tagline-size);
font-family: var(--tagline-font);
letter-spacing:3px;
text-transform:uppercase;
color:#7db7d6;]Day 4: Sandstorm — Ula’ula Southwest[/div]
Strong winds push us westward as we round Ula’ula’s southern edge and set course for Poni.


Hold tight out there.


[div=
margin-top:6px;
font-size: var(--tagline-size);
font-family: var(--tagline-font);
letter-spacing:3px;
text-transform:uppercase;
color:#7db7d6;] Day 5: Snow — South of Poni Island[/div]
Cold waters, rare conditions.


We turn northeast toward Aether Paradise.


[div=
margin-top:6px;
font-size: var(--tagline-size);
font-family: var(--tagline-font);
letter-spacing:3px;
text-transform:uppercase;
color:#7db7d6;]Day 6: Unpredictable — Aether Waters[/div]
Approaching Aether Paradise, we shift northeast again toward Melemele.


Anything can happen here, and that’s the point!


[div=
margin-top:6px;
font-size: var(--tagline-size);
font-family: var(--tagline-font);
letter-spacing:3px;
text-transform:uppercase;
color:#7db7d6;]Day 7: Melemele South — Final Approach[/div]
We linger just south of Melemele Island before docking at the ferry terminal.


Final runs. Final waves. Final marks.



